Xinerama optional: build CDE where the X libraries have no Xinerama.

CDE 2.5.3's configure stops without libXinerama, and dtwm links it through
libDtXinerama. X11R6.3, which Amix's X is, predates Xinerama (X11R6.4). The
callers already handle "no Xinerama": dtsession, dtlogin, dtfile and DtSvc
guard their own calls with USE_XINERAMA, and dtwm's WmMultiHead.c falls back
to the one screen when _DtXineramaInit returns NULL. So:
- configure.ac: a missing libXinerama is a warning; USE_XINERAMA and
  XINERAMALIB (-lXinerama) are set only when it is there;
- lib/DtXinerama: links $(XINERAMALIB); built without USE_XINERAMA,
  _DtXineramaInit returns NULL and _DtXineramaGetScreen False;
- Dt/DtXinerama.h: includes <X11/extensions/Xinerama.h> only with
  USE_XINERAMA (else <X11/Xlib.h>), and the screen list is an opaque pointer.
With libXinerama present nothing changes.

--- a/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -456,10 +456,14 @@
 AC_SEARCH_LIBS(dlopen, [dl dld], [], [])
 
 AC_CHECK_LIB(crypt, crypt)
-dnl this should be configurable, for now it is required
+dnl Xinerama is optional: without it libDtXinerama reports no Xinerama and
+dnl dtwm, dtsession, dtlogin and dtfile use the one screen
+XINERAMALIB=""
 AC_CHECK_LIB(Xinerama, XineramaQueryScreens,
-                [SOURCE_CPP_DEFINES="${SOURCE_CPP_DEFINES} -DUSE_XINERAMA"],
-                [AC_MSG_ERROR([libXinerama not found])], $X_LIBS)
+                [SOURCE_CPP_DEFINES="${SOURCE_CPP_DEFINES} -DUSE_XINERAMA"
+                 XINERAMALIB="-lXinerama"],
+                [AC_MSG_WARN([libXinerama not found: one screen only])], $X_LIBS)
+AC_SUBST(XINERAMALIB)
 
 dnl Special check for tirpc...
 AC_CHECK_LIB(tirpc, svc_register,
